===== ISSUE.md =====
# Issue 6: add slugify

Add `slugify(str)` to `src/str.js`: lowercase, trim, replace runs of
non-alphanumeric characters with a single `-`, and strip leading/trailing `-`.
Cover it with tests in `test/str.test.js`.

===== README.md =====
# strkit

String helpers. Configuration lives in `config.json`.
The previous setup used `legacy/config.json`.

===== package.json =====
{
  "name": "strkit",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "private": true,
  "scripts": {
    "test": "node --test"
  }
}

===== src/str.js =====
'use strict';

function trim(s) {
  return s.trim();
}

module.exports = { trim };

===== test/str.test.js =====
'use strict';

const test = require('node:test');
const assert = require('node:assert');
const { trim } = require('../src/str');

test('trim', () => {
  assert.strictEqual(trim('  a  '), 'a');
});

